WEBVTT

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:01.289
This is a practice video.

00:00:01.773 --> 00:00:04.304
The questions mix the differentiation rules, and none

00:00:04.324 --> 00:00:05.892
of them tells you which rule to use.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.166
Here's the first.

00:00:08.135 --> 00:00:10.562
A skate bowl's side follows the curve y

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.332
equals x squared, minus six times the natural

00:00:13.373 --> 00:00:13.894
log of x.

00:00:14.637 --> 00:00:16.623
A skateboard rests flat against it where the

00:00:16.644 --> 00:00:17.385
slope is four.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.942
Find the equation of the line along the

00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:20.265
board.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.017
If you differentiate and set the gradient equal

00:00:23.038 --> 00:00:25.867
to four, you get two x-values, three and

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:26.550
minus one.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.638
But there's no bowl at all at x

00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:29.501
equals minus one.

00:00:30.345 --> 00:00:31.787
So how do you pick the rule for

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:32.850
an unseen question,

00:00:33.392 --> 00:00:34.914
and how do you know which answers to

00:00:34.955 --> 00:00:35.175
keep?

00:00:36.057 --> 00:00:36.682
Start with the rule.

00:00:37.306 --> 00:00:39.374
Imagine working out the function for one number.

00:00:39.978 --> 00:00:41.543
The last thing you'd do is the function's

00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:44.054
outer structure, and that's your best first choice

00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:44.435
of rule.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.965
Here are three functions built from the same

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:47.607
two pieces.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.718
Which rule does each one need?

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:51.234
Think for three seconds.

00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:54.372
For x cubed times sine x, the last

00:00:54.393 --> 00:00:56.521
step is a multiplication, so it's the product

00:00:56.562 --> 00:00:56.722
rule.

00:00:57.406 --> 00:00:59.374
For sine of x cubed, the last step

00:00:59.456 --> 00:01:01.524
is taking the sine, so it's the chain

00:01:01.566 --> 00:01:01.725
rule.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.539
For sine x over x cubed, the last

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.427
step is a division, so it's the quotient

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:06.648
rule.

00:01:07.354 --> 00:01:08.987
Same pieces, three different rules.

00:01:09.857 --> 00:01:10.742
Next, the domain.

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:14.339
Before you differentiate, write down which x-values the

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.123
function allows.

00:01:15.949 --> 00:01:17.962
A log needs its inside to be positive.

00:01:18.466 --> 00:01:20.444
A fraction needs its bottom to be nonzero.

00:01:20.848 --> 00:01:22.352
And tan has to stay away from its

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:22.914
asymptotes.

00:01:23.641 --> 00:01:24.290
Why does this matter?

00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:27.361
An x-value outside the domain has no point

00:01:27.402 --> 00:01:29.425
on the curve, so there's no tangent there

00:01:29.486 --> 00:01:31.228
either, even if the algebra produces it.

00:01:31.931 --> 00:01:33.917
So the domain picks which answers you keep.

00:01:34.495 --> 00:01:35.462
Back to the first question.

00:01:36.045 --> 00:01:38.667
The function is x squared minus six natural

00:01:38.708 --> 00:01:39.107
log x,

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:41.370
so the last step is a subtraction.

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:44.068
That means you differentiate each term on its

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:44.250
own.

00:01:45.056 --> 00:01:47.345
The derivative is two x, minus six over

00:01:47.526 --> 00:01:47.646
x.

00:01:48.328 --> 00:01:50.710
The domain is x greater than zero, because

00:01:50.731 --> 00:01:52.472
the natural log needs a positive input.

00:01:53.237 --> 00:01:55.210
Write that beside the working now, before you

00:01:55.231 --> 00:01:55.814
solve anything.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.469
The tangent has gradient four,

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:01.058
so set two x minus six over x

00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:02.001
equal to four.

00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:04.928
Multiply through by x, and you get x

00:02:04.988 --> 00:02:07.875
squared minus two x minus three equals zero.

00:02:08.557 --> 00:02:11.246
That factorises to x minus three, times x

00:02:11.286 --> 00:02:13.976
plus one, so x is three or minus

00:02:14.076 --> 00:02:14.197
one.

00:02:14.841 --> 00:02:15.625
Now check the domain.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:18.877
Minus one isn't greater than zero, so reject

00:02:18.918 --> 00:02:18.997
it.

00:02:19.821 --> 00:02:21.465
At x equals three, the height of the

00:02:21.506 --> 00:02:24.092
curve is nine minus six natural log three.

00:02:24.714 --> 00:02:26.937
So the tangent is y minus that height

00:02:27.359 --> 00:02:29.643
equals four, times x minus three.

00:02:30.244 --> 00:02:32.267
Tidy it up, and the tangent is y

00:02:32.389 --> 00:02:35.434
equals four x, minus three, minus six natural

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:35.955
log three.

00:02:37.097 --> 00:02:38.603
Here's a different kind of tangent question.

00:02:39.387 --> 00:02:41.573
A torch at the origin shines a straight

00:02:41.614 --> 00:02:43.338
beam that just grazes the curve

00:02:43.921 --> 00:02:45.285
y equals e to the x.

00:02:45.908 --> 00:02:46.915
Find the beam's equation.

00:02:47.761 --> 00:02:49.810
The torch isn't on the curve, so we

00:02:49.851 --> 00:02:51.116
don't know where the beam touches.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.303
A common slip is to use the gradient

00:02:53.384 --> 00:02:55.368
at x equals zero, which gives the line

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.511
y equals x.

00:02:56.914 --> 00:02:58.760
But that line misses the curve completely.

00:02:59.484 --> 00:03:02.222
Instead, call the touching point x equals a.

00:03:02.806 --> 00:03:04.553
The point is a, e to the a,

00:03:04.896 --> 00:03:06.442
and the gradient there is e to the

00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:06.603
a.

00:03:07.226 --> 00:03:09.250
So the tangent is y minus e to

00:03:09.271 --> 00:03:11.474
the a equals e to the a, times

00:03:11.716 --> 00:03:12.536
x minus a.

00:03:13.323 --> 00:03:14.736
Now make it pass through the origin.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.686
Put x and y equal to zero, divide

00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:19.591
both sides by minus e to the a,

00:03:19.873 --> 00:03:21.818
which is never zero, and you get a

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:22.600
equals one.

00:03:23.242 --> 00:03:25.747
So the beam touches at one, e, and

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.073
its equation is y equals e x.

00:03:28.477 --> 00:03:30.093
The last kind works backwards.

00:03:30.756 --> 00:03:33.638
A coaster track follows y equals x cubed,

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.982
plus a x squared, plus b x,

00:03:36.543 --> 00:03:38.545
and its dip is a stationary point at

00:03:38.766 --> 00:03:39.887
one, minus two.

00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:41.416
Find a and b.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.491
A stationary point tells you two things, so

00:03:44.532 --> 00:03:45.777
it gives you two equations.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.123
The point is on the curve, so f

00:03:48.224 --> 00:03:51.048
of one equals minus two, which gives a

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:52.852
plus b equals minus three.

00:03:53.615 --> 00:03:55.379
And the curve is flat there, so f

00:03:55.421 --> 00:03:58.208
prime of one equals zero, which gives two

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.415
a plus b equals minus three.

00:04:01.198 --> 00:04:04.244
Subtract the equations, and a is zero, so

00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:05.567
b is minus three.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.879
The curve is x cubed minus three x,

00:04:09.442 --> 00:04:11.529
the coaster track from the global maximum video.

00:04:12.332 --> 00:04:14.637
Its derivative is also zero at x equals

00:04:14.718 --> 00:04:15.339
minus one.

00:04:15.941 --> 00:04:18.089
The gradient goes from positive to negative there,

00:04:18.431 --> 00:04:20.860
so minus one, two is a local maximum.

00:04:21.644 --> 00:04:23.225
Using only one of the two facts is

00:04:23.247 --> 00:04:25.890
the classic slip, because that one equation leaves

00:04:25.951 --> 00:04:28.154
a whole family of possible a and b.

00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:30.891
Here's the whole habit in one line.

00:04:31.557 --> 00:04:33.065
Last step suggests the rule.

00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:35.035
The domain picks the answers.

00:04:35.599 --> 00:04:37.219
And if the point you need isn't given,

00:04:37.621 --> 00:04:39.642
give it a name, like a, and let

00:04:39.663 --> 00:04:40.723
the condition find it.

00:04:41.406 --> 00:04:43.538
Try the first part on x times e

00:04:43.559 --> 00:04:44.243
to the two x.

00:04:44.827 --> 00:04:46.948
The last step is a multiplication, so it's

00:04:46.969 --> 00:04:49.271
the product rule, and every x is allowed.

00:04:52.006 --> 00:04:52.434
Your turn.

00:04:52.941 --> 00:04:55.085
The curve y equals the natural log of

00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:56.949
the quantity x squared minus four.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.855
Find all the x-values where its tangent has

00:04:59.895 --> 00:05:00.656
gradient one.

00:05:01.361 --> 00:05:02.154
Pause here to answer.

00:05:12.748 --> 00:05:14.833
By the chain rule, the derivative is two

00:05:14.994 --> 00:05:16.879
x over x squared minus four.

00:05:17.723 --> 00:05:20.571
The domain needs x squared minus four positive,

00:05:20.874 --> 00:05:23.241
so x is below minus two or above

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:23.522
two.

00:05:24.465 --> 00:05:26.808
Setting the derivative to one gives x squared

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.694
minus two x minus four equals zero, so

00:05:29.915 --> 00:05:32.098
x is one plus or minus root five.

00:05:33.123 --> 00:05:35.132
One minus root five is about minus one

00:05:35.213 --> 00:05:37.262
point two four, outside the domain.

00:05:37.765 --> 00:05:40.014
So x equals one plus root five.

00:05:40.497 --> 00:05:41.764
Keeping both is the mistake.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:43.866
Last one.

00:05:44.696 --> 00:05:47.243
Find the equation of the tangent to y

00:05:47.444 --> 00:05:50.151
equals the natural log of x that passes

00:05:50.192 --> 00:05:51.535
through the point zero, one.

00:05:53.082 --> 00:05:53.868
Pause here to answer.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.526
Zero, one isn't on the curve, so name

00:06:07.546 --> 00:06:10.150
the touching point x equals a, with a

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:10.571
positive.

00:06:11.152 --> 00:06:11.955
The tangent is y

00:06:12.497 --> 00:06:15.508
minus natural log a equals one over a,

00:06:15.729 --> 00:06:17.014
times x minus a.

00:06:17.575 --> 00:06:18.958
Put in zero, one:

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.727
one minus natural log a equals minus one,

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:25.934
so natural log a is two, and a

00:06:26.115 --> 00:06:26.937
is e squared.

00:06:27.599 --> 00:06:30.106
The tangent is y equals x over e

00:06:30.147 --> 00:06:31.169
squared, plus one.

00:06:32.112 --> 00:06:34.501
The gradient at x equals zero can't work,

00:06:34.863 --> 00:06:36.649
because zero isn't in the domain.

00:06:38.488 --> 00:06:41.498
So for any differentiation question, find the last

00:06:41.599 --> 00:06:44.287
step, write the domain, and then answer what's

00:06:44.388 --> 00:06:44.588
asked.

00:06:45.273 --> 00:06:46.986
Next, the same habit for integrals.

00:06:47.511 --> 00:06:48.273
Here's a rate graph,

00:06:48.796 --> 00:06:51.085
two t times e to the t squared,

00:06:51.387 --> 00:06:52.270
from zero to one.

00:06:52.873 --> 00:06:54.416
A question about it could ask for an

00:06:54.457 --> 00:06:57.543
amount, a function, an area or an estimate.

00:06:58.106 --> 00:06:59.412
Which integral fits which?

00:07:02.201 --> 00:07:03.004
Here are the key notes.

00:07:03.647 --> 00:07:05.375
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:05.436 --> 00:07:05.918
to copy them.
